ow us the trophy animation  when I open the game at a different  point in time so that actually kind of  worked I just removed the process of  architect and task manager and I came  back to it now and this is the first  thing that  when I got into the scenario mode so  this actually works you can end the game  with task manager and it will still give  you the animation so this is what we got  this is the trophy I actually wanted to  show this because as soon as I opened  the game I pretty much realized that  this was going to be the trophy and I  think it's a really cool trophy  definitely one of my favorites so far  especially the way that it interacts  it's not just a building that it flops  down onto the map it's really the  entrance building with that little ship  that supposedly the people would arrive  on so that's really cool we don't get  any new Maps though looks like we've got  Biscayne Beach and happy ko Harbor for  us still that said I haven't prepared  any idea of what I'm gonna do with  either of these or what's which one I'm  gonna play first so we'll just have to  see in the next video which one I chose  but for now I would like to go back to  Batavia Cay one more time to check out  what the park finally looks like all  right so here's the park in it's  slightly leggy glory this is by far the  biggest Park of the playthrough so far  and I have way more people in the park  than I expected because basically I kept  all of the rights that I was building at  the last parts of the time lapses closed  so that I wouldn't prematurely reached  the goal which I did anyway and so by  the time I reached the goal I opened all  of these rights and a slew of new guests  enter the park and now the park is super  crowded and busy that's also kind of a  good thing I guess also I'm making eight  thousand dollars a month which is by far  the most that I've ever gotten and  really kind of feels like a coaster  capital very similar to the Six Flags  Magic Mountain even with the different  types of rides that we have it's not  exactly the same but especially with  that flyer going around kind of similar  to Tatsu I think there's a slight  resemblance there so we've already seen  these parts of the park  the flying coaster now looks a little  bit better with this new flat ride here  there's this very small Q line that I  couldn't expand on just because I forgot  to add a Q line to the teacups but it  works I think besides who's gonna ride  it teacups anyway and then of course  there is the launch code  which in my personal opinion is probably  the best coaster of the park really hits  a good speed on top of that top hats  down into this Norwegian look this is  one of the smoothest inversions that  I've ever been able to make in this game  I might actually want to look at this a  little bit because this is a trick that  you might also want to use in your own  coasters I discovered it when I was  building this but I'm gonna try and make  more use of that because I've never been  able to make such a smooth diving loop  in Pike sex see that it's pretty much  the whole layout into an Immelmann at  the end and finally into the brake run  and then you get a bit of interaction as  another coaster enters the layouts so  really cool coaster actually one of my  favorite layouts of the playthrough so  far and here's again that element so I'm  sorry guys I'm gonna have to close this  the basically the way that I got to it  is that this element is slightly hard  lined which is something that you can't  really do in park text per se but it's  it's it's it's in a way kind of  different because at first what I had is  I had a setup like this where it went  straight for two tiles and then it went  upside down like this but then I  realized that if you make this one piece  realistically this wouldn't be able to  be one piece because there's just no  piece like that but Auto connects allows  you to connect these two pieces and then  you get a piece where it starts rotating  here just before it starts getting into  the curve of the loop itself and there's  something about that which is super  glossy smooth you just have to set it to  one 1/4 slope up and then you get this  really smooth roll so honestly that's I  think my new way of making this  inversion be it a dive loop or an  Immelmann I think this works really well  for either inversion so yeah really cool  I'm gonna open this again to the people  and I'm really happy with the layout  partly for that reason and then finally  we have this small flat ride Plaza over  here just a small collection of flat  rides which at all quite popular as well  you can definitely see that the park in  general is very popular because all of  these queues are filled and  all of the cycles of the flat rides are  also almost completely full  the same goes for the coaster I haven't  or all of the coasters really I haven't  seen many empty trains looking around  the park  even the pirate ship has a decent amount  of people in it and the ferris wheel too  so yeah all together really successful  Park not sure if it's my favorite  scenery wise but the the focus here was  really on the coaster layouts which I  thought was a lot of fun to do I think  this is some of the the better layouts  of the playthrough so far and yeah even  though it's not the nicest looking Park  it also has just by far the best stats  when it comes to actual gameplay really  good economy here and I just have way  more money than I know what to do with  and kind of overshot the goal of the  scenario as well so that's it for today  thank you for watching guys and I'll see  you next time in happy Co harbor or what  was the other one there was another one  anyway I'll see you Biscayne Beach  that's it  we'll see anyway see you guys next time
 

